    "source_dir": "bench-results/2026-07-25",
    "manifest_commit": "89666ce5",
    "manifest_branch": "mc/update-co-noir",
    "started_utc": "2026-07-25T11:15:40Z",
    "methodology": "Per netstats/*.json capture (one file per party per rep per phase). sent_msgs/recv_msgs/sent_bytes/recv_bytes summed across a party's peer links (up to 2 peers). party_* arrays indexed [party0, party1, party2]. total_msgs/total_bytes = sum of all party_sent + party_recv entries (counts each logical message once per side, so total is 2x message volume by design -- consistent metric, not a physical message count). median taken across successful reps (2 or 3 depending on circuit size; see bench-results/README.md rule 1). null = not measured or the cell failed/timed out/was pruned -- never fabricated, matching bench-results dataset rule 2.",
    "phase_definitions": {
      "witext": "witness extension (Rep3CoSolver.solve()) only.",
      "prove_nonzk": "combined pk-gen (both REP3 networks) + non-ZK prove (net0). Matches the split used by poseidon_prove_comms_message_fence_poseidon2sponge's PKGEN_MSGS + PROVE_MSGS (116+199=315 sent/recv per party, exactly reproduced here).",
      "prove_zk": "combined pk-gen (both REP3 networks) + ZK prove (net0)."
    },
    "known_anomalies": {
      "sha256_2e16_prove": "REP3 prove hit the 600s cell timeout (rc=124) at the SMALLEST sha256 sweep size (2^16) -- no prove netstats exist, only witext.",
      "sha256_2e17_through_2e20": "entire family pruned after the 2e16 prove timeout (bench-0_5.sh DEAD-family pruning) -- no REP3 cells attempted at all, not even witext.",
      "party_asymmetry": "bb_sha256_compression and recursion_zk show pronounced per-party sent/recv asymmetry (e.g. bb_sha256_compression prove_nonzk: p0 sent=38607/recv=51770 vs p1 sent=46926/recv=40158) -- expected for a ring topology with non-uniform per-role work, not a bug. poseidon and its 2e17-2e20 sweep are close to symmetric.",
      "inprocess_vs_cross_process_methodology_gap": "Discovered landing bb_sha256_compression_comms_band_fence_poseidon2sponge (2026-07-25): this repo's in-process LocalNetwork harness (3 std::thread::spawn 'parties' in ONE process, in-memory channels) measures SUBSTANTIALLY fewer messages AND fewer bytes than the cross-process bench run (bench-0_5.sh: 3 independent OS processes over real TCP loopback) for the SAME circuit/witness/protocol code path -- even though the resulting proof is byte-identical to the plain-prover KAT in both cases (so the MPC computation is provably correct in-process; this is a measurement-methodology gap, not a protocol bug). Measured for bb_sha256_compression non-ZK: witext 18 msgs / 640 bytes (in-process) vs 36 msgs / 3,770,048 bytes (cross-process) -- ~2x fewer msgs, ~5,891x fewer bytes; prove_nonzk (pk-gen+prove) 2,482 msgs / 1,070,633,720 bytes (in-process) vs 267,934 msgs / 17,224,995,564 bytes (cross-process) -- ~108x fewer msgs, ~16x fewer bytes. Root cause not isolated (would need to trace where the byte volume actually diverges between the two transports); hypothesis: real per-process TCP connections and/or the separate generate-witness/split-input CLI steps push more data over the wire than the in-process solve+pkgen+prove path exercises, but this is UNVERIFIED. Consequence: the cross-process `circuits` floors above are NOT valid comparanda for an in-process LocalNetwork test at this data volume -- small circuits (poseidon, add3u64, blackbox_and; see the exact-pin fences in rep3.rs) don't show this gap (their in-process pins match hand-verified sums from this same cross-process dataset, e.g. poseidon PKGEN+PROVE=315=315 exactly), so the gap appears to be a large-data-volume effect. `circuits_inprocess_baseline` below is a SEPARATE, self-consistent reference measured with the same LocalNetwork harness as the ignore-gated test that checks against it -- do not compare it to `circuits` above."
    }
  },
